  "annotations_dropped": [
    {
      "annotation_id": "c5f4bc19b060440587f5bf7e93e2ad63_28",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\n(i) Child victim/PW-1 Ms. 'Y' was one of the victims in the present case."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "a327554e9e594da9a5587e75da67779f_96",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The said letter has not been proved as per law."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "b32e4883087340edbfe6c32c4529a25f_97",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The original letter was never produced in Court or seized by IO."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "09a14cfb1cc147af879fe71e834f083a_98",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "(viii)"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "4c540a7c7a1b4169b23b782068b53a37_99",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "It is also pertinent to state that both the victims were child victims."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "942b611ab990494d8be2ce3f5f5f47c2_102",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "State Vs. Pranya Bhatia FIR 79/2021, PS Sector-23 Dwarka Page No.9 of 11 (ix) The evidence of child witnesses has to be evaluated with caution."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "437177f9e2e24252a810c1b79f2e0e32_103",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The age of child witnesses at the time of evidence was 14 and 11 years."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "3e533eb7bf954eeca29e4f87b326fea7_104",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "At the time of registration of FIR, their age was 11 and 8 years."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "a55a995953c2446db0ab7ad775f9fd16_105",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\n(x) The Indian Evidence Act, 1872 does not prescribe any particular age as a determinative factor to treat a witness to be a competent one."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "c9235be06bb54e50b0e6e30a8249bdd0_106",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "STA"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "On the contrary, Section 118 of Evidence Act envisages that all persons shall be competent to testify, unless the court considers that they are prevented from understanding the questions put to them or from giving rational answers to these "
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "d638a78ad2ab43d192cb8a96d18f80c0_107",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\n(xi) The evidence of a child witness is not required to be rejected per se, but the court as a rule of prudence considers such evidence with close scrutiny and only on being convinced about the quality thereof and reliability can record co"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "f1783a4e53f645c18b4613efbc0054fe_108",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Reliance in this regard is placed on judgment of Hon'ble Apex Court in Suryanarayana v. State of Karnataka (2001 (9) SCC 129)."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "f4ad15ccb56f466b825ca672cf672e2b_109",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\nIt was further observed by Hon'ble Supreme Court in Dattu Ramrao Sakhare v. State of Maharashtra (1997) 5 SCC 341 that:\n\"A child witness if found competent to depose to the facts and reliable one such evidence could be the basis of convict"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "0ea6864b9ed14145a8cf749e9df7d169_110",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "In other words even in the absence of oath the evidence of a child witness can be considered under Section 118 of the Evidence Act provided that such witness is able to understand the questions State Vs. Pranya Bhatia FIR 79/2021, PS Sector"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "caa8049b675a4e179d12ab2e917112b5_111",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The evidence of a child witness and credibility thereof would depend upon the circumstances of each case."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "c748a4fe9a354dd3991c94ff0ce14a35_112",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The only precaution which the court should bear in mind while assessing the evidence of a child witness is that the witness must be a reliable one and his/her demeanour must be like any other competent witness and there is no likelihood of "
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "e096cf8a1f8b41dd8f5d6efebd18e136_113",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Thus, as a rule of prudence and precaution, the prosecution was required to corroborate the version of child victims."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "48ce633d06a34334b7adc372008611c5_114",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "However, the letter which forms the basis of prosecution case has not been produced in evidence."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "2d58b070badc498083b90cd3a44c7e9f_115",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "RATIO"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Further, the testimony of child witnesses in which they have completely resiled from their previous versions cannot be relied on to prove the allegations against accused."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "7420707e04c64a1abcee4c4068a54e01_116",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "RATIO"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "In such a scenario, the accused herein is entitled to benefit of doubt."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "046fc098059946daba7a3ba52bca8749_117",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "RATIO"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "11. Accordingly, the prosecution has not been able to prove the guilt of accused in respect of offence u/s 75 JJ Act beyond reasonable doubt."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "d207742c6c834471af0371b7fb3874ca_118",
      "summary_section": "decision",
      "labels": [
        "RPC"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:decision",
        "forbidden_labels:RPC",
        "suspicious_label:rpc"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "In view of the above discussion, accused Pranya Bhatia is acquitted in the present case."
    }
  ],
